<figure class="chapter-visual two-n-map">
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创示意图：2n+1 定理的阶次账本</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original diagram: order bookkeeping for the 2n+1 theorem</span>
  </figcaption>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 880 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="two-n-title two-n-desc">
    <title id="two-n-title">Wavefunction order needed for variational energy derivatives</title>
    <desc id="two-n-desc">
      A horizontal order axis shows that the unperturbed wavefunction gives first-order energy, first-order wavefunction information gives energy through third order, and second-order wavefunction information gives energy through fifth order. Higher wavefunction corrections cancel through stationarity and normalization, not because they vanish.
    </desc>
    <line x1="90" y1="200" x2="810" y2="200" class="two-n-map__axis" />
    {[0,1,2,3,4,5].map((order) => (
      <g>
        <line x1={110 + order * 135} y1="190" x2={110 + order * 135} y2="210" class="two-n-map__tick" />
        <text x={110 + order * 135} y="236" text-anchor="middle">order {order}</text>
      </g>
    ))}

    <rect x="92" y="56" width="145" height="72" rx="10" class="two-n-map__psi" />
    <text x="164" y="84" text-anchor="middle">known ψ⁽⁰⁾</text>
    <text x="164" y="108" text-anchor="middle">energy through 1</text>
    <path d="M164 128 L164 174 L245 174" class="two-n-map__connector" />

    <rect x="258" y="56" width="220" height="72" rx="10" class="two-n-map__psi" />
    <text x="368" y="84" text-anchor="middle">known ψ⁽⁰⁾, ψ⁽¹⁾</text>
    <text x="368" y="108" text-anchor="middle">energy through 3</text>
    <path d="M368 128 L368 158 L515 158 L515 174" class="two-n-map__connector" />

    <rect x="500" y="56" width="285" height="72" rx="10" class="two-n-map__psi two-n-map__psi--accent" />
    <text x="642" y="84" text-anchor="middle">known ψ⁽⁰⁾, ψ⁽¹⁾, ψ⁽²⁾</text>
    <text x="642" y="108" text-anchor="middle">energy through 5</text>
    <path d="M642 128 L642 144 L785 144 L785 174" class="two-n-map__connector" />

    <text x="440" y="278" text-anchor="middle">energy order = 2n + 1 when wavefunction is known through order n</text>
  </svg>

  <div class="two-n-map__fallback">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Known wavefunction orders</th><th>Energy order fixed by stationarity</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0–1</td><td>3</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0–2</td><td>5</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>高阶态修正并非等于零；它们在满足本征方程、归一化和变分驻值条件后，从目标能量阶次中消去。</p>
    <p lang="en">Higher-order state corrections are not zero; they cancel from the target energy order after the eigen-equation, normalization, and variational stationarity conditions are imposed.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>学习目的：</strong>把“已知波函数到 $n$ 阶”与“能量可确定到 $2n+1$ 阶”分开，避免把定理误读为高阶波函数修正不存在。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Learning purpose:</strong> separate knowledge of the wavefunction through order $n$ from determination of the energy through order $2n+1$, avoiding the false claim that higher-order wavefunction corrections do not exist.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong><code>n=0→1</code>、<code>n=1→3</code>、<code>n=2→5</code> 三个阶次映射同时出现在图和表中。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the mappings <code>n=0→1</code>, <code>n=1→3</code>, and <code>n=2→5</code> appear in both the diagram and table.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>定理要求目标能量泛函在约束下驻值；它不保证 perturbation series 收敛，也不消除 basis、SCF 或 observable 的数值收敛问题。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> the theorem requires constrained stationarity of the target energy functional; it does not guarantee convergence of the perturbation series or remove basis, SCF, or observable convergence requirements.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

